  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Ecuador 2023 (DRRS23EC05)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The official request comes from the Secretar&#xED;a de Gesti&#xF3;n de Riesgos de la Rep&#xFA;blica del Ecuador, the responsible ministry for disaster risk management in Ecuador.The request asks for specific assistance due to the effects of the El Ni&#xF1;o-phenomenon, and suggests to focus this assistance either on coastal erosion or flood risk. This mission will focus on coastal erosion.The specific problem of coastal erosion in Ecuador refers to the gradual loss of land and beaches due to the action of the sea and natural processes. The experts can contribute by providing specialised advice in coastal engineering techniques and beach design, territorial planning to mitigate erosion, protect the coast and ensure the sustainability of coastal areas.</narrative>
  </description>
